the folder is empty. The same happened in packages/{core,webview}/node_modules/.vite-temp, which are inside packages.\n- **REPO/.git.** Its directory timestamp changes when git status takes its index lock. My git use was read-only (status, diff, show); there is no content change. The latest change, at 13:33:44, came after my last git command, so something else (probably VS Code's git) does this too.\n- **The user journal** logs the transient scopes that capped.sh's `systemd-run --user --scope` creates.\n\n**What did not change**\n- No new entries in /tmp/node-compile-cache (compile cache disabled).\n- No /tmp/playwright-transform-cache-1000 (PWTEST_CACHE_DIR was in scratch).\n- No writes to REPO/node_modules/.vitest-cache.\n- Nothing written to packages/extension/dist or packages/extension/out (checked).\n- No packages/webview/test-results folder.\n\n**Changed, but not by me**\n- docs/slice2-plan.md, at 13:30:06 and 13:33:17, by another writer (the slice-2 planning). I did not edit it.\n- VS Code (~/.config/Code), Vivaldi, Discord, Copilot (~/.cache/copilot, ~/.copilot), tracker3.\n- Claude Code's own files (~/.claude.json, ~/.claude/backups, projects, skills). I read no credentials.\n- System logs and services (/var/log, anacron, ds_agent, fail2ban, timesync).\n\n**Blocked command.** The safety check blocked one command, a compound of `rm -rf $F/webview-build-mut && cp …`. Nothing ran: the folder did not exist. I then copied without any removal.\n\n**What I did not do.** No network, no installs, no change to git state, no real Claude (CAP sets TELELEAN_NO_REAL_CLAUDE=1), and no Lean run. None of my processes is left.\n\n**Left in scratch.** F/webview-build-mut and F/pw-output-mut, from the mutation check, can be deleted.\n\n======================================================================\n5. THE SLICES (the user's question)\n======================================================================\nFrom docs/slice1-plan.md:\n\n**Slice 1: the new board (spec v4)*